WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:01.338
Hi, I'm Wainscot!

00:00:01.338 --> 00:00:04.889
Need for Speed Most Wanted now runs in a browser tab, and

00:00:04.889 --> 00:00:06.369
nobody had its source code.

00:00:06.369 --> 00:00:06.961
So how?

00:00:08.225 --> 00:00:12.427
The idea: translate the game's own executable to WebAssembly once, ahead of

00:00:12.427 --> 00:00:14.879
time, and rebuild the Windows it calls.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:19.244
Start with the executable a player installs.

00:00:19.244 --> 00:00:22.735
A disassembler finds every function and jump target in it.

00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:25.647
Each is translated once, at build time.

00:00:25.647 --> 00:00:28.138
The names are the disassembler's, never EA's.

00:00:28.558 --> 00:00:30.177
Out comes one WebAssembly module.

00:00:30.177 --> 00:00:32.444
There is no just in time compiler.

00:00:32.864 --> 00:00:37.256
The game still calls Windows, so a host answers: threads, exceptions, input,

00:00:37.256 --> 00:00:40.184
and Direct three D nine, drawn with WebGPU.

00:00:41.692 --> 00:00:44.734
Translating ahead of time has two classic failure points.

00:00:45.154 --> 00:00:48.323
A jump to a computed address must land on a block

00:00:48.323 --> 00:00:49.476
the translator already knows.

00:00:49.896 --> 00:00:52.609
And an instruction it does not model must never run.

00:00:53.029 --> 00:00:54.560
Old mods patched bytes.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:57.238
Here, fixes replace whole functions by address.

00:00:58.592 --> 00:01:00.706
Only the executable is copied whole.

00:01:00.706 --> 00:01:03.526
Every other file stays on a third-party CDN.

00:01:03.946 --> 00:01:07.601
When the game reads, the tab fetches eight megabyte blocks and keeps them.

00:01:08.021 --> 00:01:10.434
The game just sees a folder under Program Files.

00:01:12.092 --> 00:01:18.487
42,545 addresses inside speed.exe in the symbol table it ships.

00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:24.226
The GTA Five port compiled the engine's own source, names and all,

00:01:24.226 --> 00:01:25.959
and swapped its platform layer.

00:01:26.379 --> 00:01:28.448
This one had only the executable.

00:01:28.448 --> 00:01:32.585
So it runs exactly the original code, and rebuilds Windows around it.

00:01:33.808 --> 00:01:36.771
With no source, the game's own logic survives exactly.

00:01:36.771 --> 00:01:41.051
The hard work moves to the edges: Windows, the shaders and the files.

00:01:42.692 --> 00:01:44.468
The executable, translated once.

00:01:44.468 --> 00:01:46.244
Windows, rebuilt on WebGPU.

00:01:46.244 --> 00:01:50.240
And the game's files, streamed from someone else's server.

00:01:50.660 --> 00:01:52.822
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:52.822 --> 00:01:53.439
I'm Wainscot.

00:01:53.439 --> 00:01:53.748
Bye!
